{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"theory-type","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"Types over an Algebraic Theory"}]},"title_text":"Types over an Algebraic Theory","kind":"definition","taxon":null,"url":"theory-type.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","theory-type"],["kind","definition"],["label","Definition"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Fix a finitary algebraic theory "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":": sorts "},{"Math":{"src":"S"}},{"Text":", a signature "},{"Math":{"src":"sigma"}},{"Text":", equations, and a set "},{"Math":{"src":"V"}},{"Text":" of generators. Write "},{"Math":{"src":"bold(M)"}},{"Text":" for the free "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":"-model on "},{"Math":{"src":"V"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"|bold(M)|_s"}},{"Text":" for its carrier at sort "},{"Math":{"src":"s"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"A "},{"Emph":[{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":"-type"}]},{"Text":" of sort "},{"Math":{"src":"s"}},{"Text":" is a family "},{"Math":{"src":"A : |bold(M)|_s -> sans(\"Type\")"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"For "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":"-types "},{"Math":{"src":"A"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"B"}},{"Text":" of sort "},{"Math":{"src":"s"}},{"Text":" we have the additives, defined pointwise,"}]},{"Math":{"src":"(A class(\"binary\", \\&) B)(m) = A(m) times B(m), quad (A ⊕ B)(m) = A(m) + B(m), quad\n  (A => B)(m) = A(m) -> B(m),"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"along with "},{"Math":{"src":"top"}},{"Text":", "},{"Math":{"src":"bot"}},{"Text":", and their indexed versions."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Each operation "},{"Math":{"src":"o : s_0, ..., s_(n-1) -> s"}},{"Text":" of "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":" gives a multiplicative, defined by "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"day-convolution","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"Day convolution"}]}},{"Text":","}]},{"Math":{"src":"⊗[o](A_0, ..., A_(n-1))(m) = Sigma_(o(m_0, ..., m_(n-1)) = m) times Pi_(i < n) A_i (m_i)."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Each lifted operation also has closed structure: a residual in each of its arguments. Day algebras "},{"Cite":{"key":"robinson_wrigley_2026","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":" give a more general convolutional definition."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"When "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":" is the theory of monoids and "},{"Math":{"src":"V"}},{"Text":" is an alphabet, "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(T)"}},{"Text":"-types are formal grammars. Multiplication gives "},{"Math":{"src":"⊗"}},{"Text":", the unit gives "},{"Math":{"src":"epsilon"}},{"Text":", and we recover Lambek"},{"Math":{"src":"\"\"^mono(D)"}},{"Text":"."}]}]}}}]}}
